      "Needs a 120 V, 20 A circuit according to both dealer listings",
      "Seven years on the frame and motor is short for a commercial machine; parts are two years",
      "Unit weight conflicts between listings (358.7 lb and 433 lb)",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The Freemotion for a home buyer who wants a commercial AC treadmill with a plain console and the brand’s lowest price, and has a 20-amp circuit for it.",
    description: "The t8.9b is Freemotion’s entry commercial treadmill. Two authorised US dealers, US MedRehab and Wellbots, agree on a 4.0 HP AC commercial drive motor, a 21.5 by 60-inch two-sided cushioned deck, 0 to 12 mph, 0 to 15% incline, a 400 lb maximum user weight and a 120 V, 20 A power requirement, and TreadmillReviewGuru gives the same motor and deck. The console has 1-Step speed and incline keys, dual-grip and Polar heart-rate support, a USB charging port and onboard programmes including Army, Navy, Marine Corps, Air Force and fire-service fitness tests. Both dealers list seven years on the frame and drive motor, two on parts and console and one of labour. The listings disagree on weight: 358.7 lb at one, 433 lb at the other. On 5 November 2026 Wellbots listed it at $5,999, US MedRehab at $7,300 and Freemotion’s home store at $7,799.",
  },
  {
    id: "freemotion-t10-9b-reflex",
    name: "Freemotion t10.9b Reflex",
    brand: "Freemotion",
    category: "Reflex-Deck Commercial Treadmill, No Touchscreen",
    badge: "Best Value Reflex",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=commercial+treadmill&tag=sktiger-20",
    amazonLabel: "Shop Similar on Amazon",
    image: null,
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$8,999-$9,400 (Freemotion home store and dealer, 5 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":8999,"high":9400},
    specs: "21.5 x 60 in. Reflex deck · 5.0 HP AC · 0-12 mph · 0-15% incline · 400 lb max user · 487 lb",
    pros: [
      "The Reflex cushioned deck used in Orangetheory-style studio treadmills",
      "A 5.0 HP AC drive motor, the largest rating in the range alongside the t22.9",
      "A 400 lb user rating on a heavy 487 lb frame",
      "Non-touch console with 1-Step keys; pair a phone or tablet for iFIT if you want it",
    ],
    cons: [
