      "At 87.7 inches long it needs a deep room",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The Freemotion most home buyers should consider first: the Reflex deck and the big AC motor without paying for the t22.9’s screen.",
    description: "The t10.9b is the cheaper of Freemotion’s two Reflex treadmills. An authorised dealer, US MedRehab, lists a 5.0 HP AC commercial drive motor, a 21.5 by 60-inch running surface on the two-sided Reflex cushioning deck, 0 to 12 mph, 0 to 15% incline, a 400 lb maximum user weight, a weight of 487 lb and a footprint of 87.7 by 34 by 66 inches; Garage Gym Reviews gives the same motor, deck, top speed, user weight, weight and footprint. The console shows speed, incline, pace, vertical feet and heart rate with EKG grips, and has a USB port, audio out and a TV input; there is no touchscreen. US MedRehab lists seven years on frame and motor, two on parts, two on the console and one of labour in the US; Garage Gym Reviews gives one year on the console, so check. Freemotion’s home store listed it at $8,999 (shown against $12,999) on 5 November 2026, and US MedRehab at $9,400.",
